                        INTRODUCTION
                    </div>

                    <p>The effects of the 1994 Genocide against the Tutsi left Rwanda’s economy in ruins, with the business community particularly hard-hit.</p>

                    <p>The few formal businesses that existed were inefficient and severely under-resourced. However, post-genocide socioeconomic reforms, including the establishment of PSF in 1999, have revitalized the private sector, transforming it into a key driver of Rwanda’s Vision 2020 and beyond.</p>
                    
                    <p>Today, the private sector leads the employment rate at 94% and contributes almost 60% to the annual national budget through taxes.</p>
